# tieout — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values. Never commit `.env`.
# `.gitignore` ignores `.env` / `.env.*` but keeps this `.env.example` template.
#
# --- Mainnet RPC (Batch 2: derivation, verify, live-verify gates) -----------
#
# REQUIREMENT: a mainnet *archive* endpoint. tieout reads historical state at
# pinned old blocks — wstETH.stEthPerToken() at rebase blocks, Chainlink
# getRoundData(roundId)/decimals() at the pinned round, getBlock(n).timestamp.
# A pruned/full node (~128 blocks of state) will fail these reads.
#
# A free Alchemy key includes unrestricted archive access. Note the free tier
# caps eth_getLogs at a 10-block range per request, so the heavy verify
# re-fetch / CI harness prefer a small window or a higher-range endpoint
# (dRPC / PublicNode allow ~10k-block ranges); the live-verify gates are point
# reads and run fine on the free tier.

# Used by `cast` (foundry) and the `tieout verify` CLI (packages/recon).
ETH_RPC_URL=https://eth-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_KEY_HERE

# Used by the Ponder live adapter (packages/indexer/ponder.config.ts, chainId 1).
# Point it at the same archive endpoint as ETH_RPC_URL.
PONDER_RPC_URL_1=https://eth-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_KEY_HERE
